# Paired with canonical_reduced.bvnr: the same quantities spelled with prefixes
# and with a repeated base. `bovnar pretty-print --canonical` must fold both to
# byte-identical output -- that convergence is the whole claim of the mode.
#
# The mode normalises a RESCALED float back into float shape (BVN_NUM_CANONICAL),
# which is why 5.0 km lands on "5000.0 m" and not "5000 m" -- otherwise it would
# not agree with the file beside it, which wrote metres directly.
#
# What it does NOT do is rewrite a literal no rescale touched. A document that
# writes "5000" where this one writes "5000.0" still differs, and float_dec
# trailing zeros are left alone on purpose: 0.250 and 0.25 are not
# interchangeable in that family, so collapsing them would discard what the
# producer said about precision. Full number-shape canonicalisation is a larger
# change than unit reduction and is not attempted here.
.dist  = <float:64,k~m> 5.0;
.area  = <float:64,m·m> 2.0;
.speed = <float:64,k~m/h> 90.0;
.mass  = <float_dec:64,k~g> 0.25;
